meta {
  name: Upload File
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/files
  body: multipartForm
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{access_token}}
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

body:multipart-form {
  file: @file()
  context: logo
}

docs {
  ## Purpose

  Uploads a file. Select a synthetic local file in Bruno before sending.

  ## Authentication

  A logo upload requires a system administrator or `settings.update`.
  A content cover upload uses `context: contents` and requires a system administrator, `contents.create`, or `contents.update`.

  ## Behavior

  Context uploads are public and use the smaller of the configured context size and the server upload limit.
  A cover must decode as AVIF, GIF, JPEG, PNG or WebP and match its declared media type. Covers can contain up to 67,108,864 pixels across all frames.
  Existing clients may send `visibility: public` or `visibility: private` without a context.
  Legacy public uploads require a system administrator or `settings.update`.
  Private uploads require authentication and return no public URL.

  ## Response

  - `201 Created` — File stored successfully. The response contains the ID, byte size, initial usage, content type, visibility and public URL when available.
  - `400 Bad Request` — File, context or visibility is invalid.
  - `401 Unauthorized` — Authentication is missing or invalid.
  - `403 Forbidden` — Public upload is not allowed.
  - `408 Request Timeout` — The request body is still incomplete after the 60-second read deadline.
  - `413 Content Too Large` — The file exceeds its limit or the complete multipart body exceeds that limit plus 64 KiB of framing and metadata.
  - `415 Unsupported Media Type` — Content-Type is not multipart/form-data, or the cover image is invalid, unsupported, or does not match its declared media type.
  - `503 Service Unavailable` — Four uploads are already in progress in this process. An authenticated request is rejected before body reading, with `Cache-Control: no-store`.
}
